IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc16-officials.l4 -- sections 483 to 485.2 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (Part XV, General Powers of Certain Officials,
-- procedural irregularities, recommencement after dismissal for want of prosecution, and the summons under the Identification of Criminals Act).
-- Part agent ccc16. Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Imports the keel's core only.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- How a result reads (NOTES.md, Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING): `JUST TRUE` the text's own words cover the case;
-- `JUST FALSE` the text says no ("is not lost", "shall not", "only if", "must", "without", a failed "where" or a period the text fixes);
-- `NOTHING` not covered (a power whose "if" gate fails, a limit the section puts on a grant, silence).
-- Conventions taken here, each flagged in NOTES.md (fork register, marginal readings):
--   * a power named "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12);
--   * a "where" gate that fails, and a period the text fixes, answer JUST FALSE (rulings (a) and (b) of 2026-11-05), counted in the fork register;
--   * a "must" requirement not met answers JUST FALSE (case by case, the maintainer, 2026-11-05).

§ `Section 483 -- Officials with powers of two justices`

-- A judge or provincial court judge authorized by the law of the province may do alone what the Code authorizes two or more justices to do.
-- A power named "may": every fact is a gate of "authorized ... to do anything that is required to be done by two or more justices", so a failed gate is NOTHING.
-- src:8723 | 483 Every judge or provincial court judge authorized by the law of the province in which he is appointed to do anything that is required to be done by two or more justices may do alone anything that this Act or any other Act of Parliament authorizes two or more justices to do.
@ref s 483 (src:8723)
GIVEN `the person is a judge or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized by the law of the province in which they are appointed to do anything that is required to be done by two or more justices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is something this Act or any other Act of Parliament authorizes two or more justices to do` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 483 the judge or provincial court judge may do alone what two or more justices are authorized to do` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a judge or provincial court judge`
      AND `the person is authorized by the law of the province in which they are appointed to do anything that is required to be done by two or more justices`
      AND `the thing is something this Act or any other Act of Parliament authorizes two or more justices to do`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every judge or provincial court judge authorized by the law of the province in which he is appointed to do anything that is required to be done by two or more justices may do alone"

§ `Section 484 -- Preserving order in court`

-- src:8725 | 484 Every judge or provincial court judge has the same power and authority to preserve order in a court over which he presides as may be exercised by the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province during the sittings thereof.
@ref s 484 (src:8725)
GIVEN `the person is a judge or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person presides over the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 484 the judge or provincial court judge has the same power and authority to preserve order as the superior court of criminal jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge or provincial court judge` AND `the person presides over the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in a court over which he presides"

§ `Section 485 -- Procedural irregularities`

-- 485(1) Jurisdiction over an offence is not lost by reason of a failure to act at a particular time or of a failure to comply with the provisions on adjournments or remands.
-- The answer is "jurisdiction over the offence is lost by reason of the failure": JUST FALSE for the two failures the text names; NOTHING for any other reason.
-- src:8726 | Procedural irregularities
-- src:8727 | 485 (1) Jurisdiction over an offence is not lost by reason of the failure of any court, judge, provincial court judge or justice to act in the exercise of that jurisdiction at any particular time, or by reason of a failure to comply with any of the provisions of this Act respecting adjournments or remands.
@ref s 485(1) (src:8726-8727)
GIVEN `the failure is a failure of a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice to act in the exercise of that jurisdiction at any particular time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is a failure to comply with a provision of this Act respecting adjournments or remands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(1) jurisdiction over the offence is lost by reason of the failure` MEANS
    IF    `the failure is a failure of a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice to act in the exercise of that jurisdiction at any particular time`
       OR `the failure is a failure to comply with a provision of this Act respecting adjournments or remands`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Jurisdiction over an offence is not lost by reason of the failure of any court, judge, provincial court judge or justice to act in the exercise of that jurisdiction at any particular time"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says nothing of other reasons

-- 485(1.1) Jurisdiction over an accused is not lost by reason of the failure of the accused to appear personally or in person, so long as the provisions
-- of this Act or a rule made under section 482 or 482.1 permitting the accused not to appear personally or in person apply.
-- src:8728 | When accused not appearing personally or in person
-- src:8729 | (1.1) Jurisdiction over an accused is not lost by reason of the failure of the accused to appear personally or in person, so long as the provisions of this Act or a rule made under section 482 or 482.1 permitting the accused not to appear personally or in person apply.
@ref s 485(1.1) (src:8728-8729)
GIVEN `the accused failed to appear personally or in person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of this Act or a rule made under section 482 or 482.1 permitting the accused not to appear personally or in person apply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(1.1) jurisdiction over the accused is lost by reason of the failure to appear personally or in person` MEANS
    IF    `the accused failed to appear personally or in person`
      AND `the provisions of this Act or a rule made under section 482 or 482.1 permitting the accused not to appear personally or in person apply`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Jurisdiction over an accused is not lost by reason of the failure of the accused to appear personally or in person, so long as"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "so long as the provisions of this Act or a rule made under section 482 or 482.1 permitting the accused not to appear personally or in person apply"

-- 485(2) Where jurisdiction over an accused or a defendant is lost and has not been regained, a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may, within three
-- months after the loss of jurisdiction, issue a summons or, if it or he considers it necessary in the public interest, a warrant for the arrest.
-- "within three months after the loss of jurisdiction": the last day is the day three calendar months after the day of the loss (a period the text fixes: ruling (a) of 2026-11-05).
GIVEN `the day jurisdiction was lost` IS A DATE
      `the day the issue is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 485(2) the issue is within three months after the loss of jurisdiction` MEANS
        `the day the issue is made` AT LEAST `the day jurisdiction was lost`
    AND `the day the issue is made` AT MOST (`add months` `the day jurisdiction was lost` 3)

-- src:8730 | Summons or warrant
-- src:8731 | (2) Where jurisdiction over an accused or a defendant is lost and has not been regained, a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may, within three months after the loss of jurisdiction, issue a summons, or if it or he considers it necessary in the public interest, a warrant for the arrest of the accused or defendant.
@ref s 485(2) (summons) (src:8730-8731)
GIVEN `jurisdiction over the accused or defendant is lost and has not been regained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day jurisdiction was lost` IS A DATE
      `the day the summons is issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(2) the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may issue a summons` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `jurisdiction over the accused or defendant is lost and has not been regained`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where jurisdiction over an accused or a defendant is lost and has not been regained"
        IF (NOT `s 485(2) the issue is within three months after the loss of jurisdiction` `the day jurisdiction was lost` `the day the summons is issued`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within three months after the loss of jurisdiction"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8730 | Summons or warrant
-- src:8731 | (2) Where jurisdiction over an accused or a defendant is lost and has not been regained, a court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may, within three months after the loss of jurisdiction, issue a summons, or if it or he considers it necessary in the public interest, a warrant for the arrest of the accused or defendant.
@ref s 485(2) (warrant for arrest) (src:8730-8731)
GIVEN `jurisdiction over the accused or defendant is lost and has not been regained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day jurisdiction was lost` IS A DATE
      `the day the warrant is issued` IS A DATE
      `the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice considers the warrant necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(2) the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may issue a warrant for the arrest` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `jurisdiction over the accused or defendant is lost and has not been regained`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where jurisdiction over an accused or a defendant is lost and has not been regained"
        IF (NOT `s 485(2) the issue is within three months after the loss of jurisdiction` `the day jurisdiction was lost` `the day the warrant is issued`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within three months after the loss of jurisdiction"
        IF (NOT `the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice considers the warrant necessary in the public interest`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it or he considers it necessary in the public interest, a warrant for the arrest of the accused or defendant"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 485(3) Where no summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2) within the period provided therein, the proceedings shall be deemed to be dismissed for want
-- of prosecution and shall not be recommenced except in accordance with section 485.1.
-- The deeming takes effect when the three months have passed with nothing issued: asked as of a day, with the day a summons or warrant was issued (if one was).
-- src:8732 | Dismissal for want of prosecution
-- src:8733 | (3) Where no summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2) within the period provided therein, the proceedings shall be deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution and shall not be recommenced except in accordance with section 485.1.
@ref s 485(3) (deemed dismissal) (src:8732-8733)
GIVEN `the day jurisdiction was lost` IS A DATE
      `the day a summons or warrant was issued under subsection (2), if one was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(3) the proceedings are deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day a summons or warrant was issued under subsection (2), if one was`
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF `s 485(2) the issue is within three months after the loss of jurisdiction` `the day jurisdiction was lost` issued
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where no summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2) within the period provided therein" (one was issued within the period)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        IF `the day the question is asked` GREATER THAN (`add months` `the day jurisdiction was lost` 3)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within the period provided therein" (the period has not yet run out)

-- "shall not be recommenced except in accordance with section 485.1": the answer of s 485.1 (is a new information or indictment barred?) is taken as an input.
-- Barred (JUST TRUE) means not recommenced; where the consent or order of s 485.1 is present the exception is met and the subsection says nothing more; where the proceedings
-- were not deemed dismissed under the subsection it is silent.
-- src:8732 | Dismissal for want of prosecution
-- src:8733 | (3) Where no summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2) within the period provided therein, the proceedings shall be deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution and shall not be recommenced except in accordance with section 485.1.
@ref s 485(3) (recommencement) (src:8732-8733)
GIVEN `the proceedings are deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution under subsection 485(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 485.1 on whether a new information or a new indictment is barred` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(3) the proceedings may be recommenced` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the proceedings are deemed to be dismissed for want of prosecution under subsection 485(3)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of proceedings deemed dismissed under it
    ELSE CONSIDER `the answer of s 485.1 on whether a new information or a new indictment is barred`
         WHEN JUST barred THEN
             IF barred
             THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not be recommenced except in accordance with section 485.1"
             ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in accordance with section 485.1" (section 485.1 does not bar on these facts, and the subsection grants nothing)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in accordance with section 485.1" (the consent or order of section 485.1 is present, or its answer is not given)

-- 485(4) Where, in the opinion of the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice, an accused or a defendant who appears at a proceeding has been misled or prejudiced
-- by reason of any matter referred to in subsection (1), the court ... may adjourn the proceeding and may make such order as it or he considers appropriate.
-- src:8734 | Adjournment and order
-- src:8735 | (4) Where, in the opinion of the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice, an accused or a defendant who appears at a proceeding has been misled or prejudiced by reason of any matter referred to in subsection (1), the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may adjourn the proceeding and may make such order as it or he considers appropriate.
@ref s 485(4) (src:8734-8735)
GIVEN `the accused or defendant appears at the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice, the accused or defendant has been misled or prejudiced by reason of a matter referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(4) the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice may adjourn the proceeding and make an order` MEANS
    IF    `the accused or defendant appears at the proceeding`
      AND `in the opinion of the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice, the accused or defendant has been misled or prejudiced by reason of a matter referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in the opinion of the court, judge, provincial court judge or justice, an accused or a defendant who appears at a proceeding has been misled or prejudiced by reason of any matter referred to in subsection (1)"

-- 485(5) The provisions of Part XVI apply with such modifications as the circumstances require where a summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2).
-- src:8736 | Part XVI to apply
-- src:8737 | (5) The provisions of Part XVI apply with such modifications as the circumstances require where a summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2).
@ref s 485(5) (src:8736-8737)
GIVEN `a summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485(5) the provisions of Part XVI apply with such modifications as the circumstances require` MEANS
    IF `a summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a summons or warrant is issued under subsection (2)"

§ `Section 485.1 -- Recommencement where dismissal for want of prosecution`

-- Where an indictment in respect of a transaction is dismissed (or deemed dismissed) for want of prosecution, a new information shall not be laid and a new indictment shall not be preferred
-- in respect of the same transaction without (a) the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General, in a prosecution conducted by the Attorney General or in which
-- the Attorney General intervenes; or (b) the written order of a judge of that court, in any other prosecution. The answer is the bar: JUST TRUE where no (a) or (b) is present.
-- src:8738 | Recommencement where dismissal for want of prosecution
-- src:8739 | 485.1 Where an indictment in respect of a transaction is dismissed or deemed by any provision of this Act to be dismissed for want of prosecution, a new information shall not be laid and a new indictment shall not be preferred before any court in respect of the same transaction without
-- src:8740 | (a) the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General, in any prosecution conducted by the Attorney General or in which the Attorney General intervenes; or
-- src:8741 | (b) the written order of a judge of that court, in any prosecution conducted by a prosecutor other than the Attorney General and in which the Attorney General does not intervene.
@ref s 485.1 (a), (b) (src:8738-8741)
GIVEN `an indictment in respect of the transaction is dismissed or deemed by a provision of this Act to be dismissed for want of prosecution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General conducts the prosecution or intervenes in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General has given personal consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a judge of that court has made a written order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485.1 a new information or a new indictment in respect of the same transaction is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `an indictment in respect of the transaction is dismissed or deemed by a provision of this Act to be dismissed for want of prosecution`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an indictment in respect of a transaction is dismissed or deemed by any provision of this Act to be dismissed for want of prosecution"
        IF (`the Attorney General conducts the prosecution or intervenes in it` AND `the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General has given personal consent in writing`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without (a) the personal consent in writing of the Attorney General or Deputy Attorney General"
        IF ((NOT `the Attorney General conducts the prosecution or intervenes in it`) AND `a judge of that court has made a written order`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) the written order of a judge of that court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 485.2 -- Summons -- Identification of Criminals Act`

-- 485.2(1) A justice or judge may, on application in writing and on oath in Form 6.1, issue a summons, in Form 6.2, requiring an accused or offender to appear ... for the purposes of the
-- Identification of Criminals Act if (a) the accused is charged with, or the offender has been determined to be guilty of, an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act;
-- (b) the accused or offender was previously required to appear for the purposes of that Act and the measurements, processes or operations were not completed; and
-- (c) the justice or judge is satisfied that the reasons for their not having been completed were exceptional. Subsection (5)'s alternative (a writing by telecommunication) is taken as the application.
-- src:8742 | Summons — Identification of Criminals Act
-- src:8743 | 485.2 (1) A justice or judge may, on application in writing and on oath in Form 6.1, issue a summons, in Form 6.2, requiring an accused or offender to appear at a time and place stated in it for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act if
-- src:8744 | (a) the accused is charged with, or the offender has been determined to be guilty of, an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of that Act;
-- src:8745 | (b) the accused or offender was previously required to appear for the purposes of that Act and the measurements, processes or operations referred to in that Act were not completed; and
-- src:8746 | (c) the justice or judge is satisfied that the reasons for the measurements, processes or operations not having been completed were exceptional.
@ref s 485.2(1) (a), (b), (c) (src:8742-8746)
GIVEN `the application is in writing and on oath in Form 6.1, or is made by a means of telecommunication under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is charged with, or the offender has been determined to be guilty of, an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused or offender was previously required to appear for the purposes of that Act and the measurements, processes or operations referred to in that Act were not completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice or judge is satisfied that the reasons for the measurements, processes or operations not having been completed were exceptional` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485.2(1) a justice or judge may issue a summons requiring the accused or offender to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` MEANS
    IF    `the application is in writing and on oath in Form 6.1, or is made by a means of telecommunication under subsection (5)`
      AND `the accused is charged with, or the offender has been determined to be guilty of, an offence referred to in paragraph 2(1)(c) of the Identification of Criminals Act`
      AND `the accused or offender was previously required to appear for the purposes of that Act and the measurements, processes or operations referred to in that Act were not completed`
      AND `the justice or judge is satisfied that the reasons for the measurements, processes or operations not having been completed were exceptional`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, on application in writing and on oath in Form 6.1, issue a summons"

-- 485.2(2) Subsection (1) applies in respect of an offender only if proceedings are ongoing in relation to the matter ... and for which the sentencing proceedings have not concluded.
-- For an accused the subsection is silent.
-- src:8747 | Limitation
-- src:8748 | (2) Subsection (1) applies in respect of an offender only if proceedings are ongoing in relation to the matter for which they were previously required to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act and for which the sentencing proceedings have not concluded.
@ref s 485.2(2) (src:8747-8748)
GIVEN `the person is an offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings are ongoing in relation to the matter for which the offender was previously required to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sentencing proceedings for that matter have not concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485.2(2) subsection (1) applies in respect of the offender` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is an offender`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the limitation speaks only of an offender
    ELSE IF `proceedings are ongoing in relation to the matter for which the offender was previously required to appear for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act` AND `the sentencing proceedings for that matter have not concluded`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies in respect of an offender only if proceedings are ongoing"

-- 485.2(3) The application must state the reasons why the measurements, processes or operations were not completed.
-- src:8749 | Reasons
-- src:8750 | (3) The application must state the reasons why the measurements, processes or operations were not completed.
@ref s 485.2(3) (src:8749-8750)
GIVEN `the application states the reasons why the measurements, processes or operations were not completed` IS A BOOLEAN
