`s 485.2(5) the application may be made by the means of telecommunication` MEANS
    IF `the means of telecommunication produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any means of telecommunication that produces a writing"

-- 485.2(6) A person who uses a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (5) may, instead of swearing an oath, make a statement in writing stating that all matters contained
-- in the application are true to their knowledge and belief, and that statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath.
-- src:8755 | Alternative to oath
-- src:8756 | (6) A person who uses a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (5) may, instead of swearing an oath, make a statement in writing stating that all matters contained in the application are true to their knowledge and belief, and that statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath.
@ref s 485.2(6) (the alternative to an oath) (src:8755-8756)
GIVEN `the person uses a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is in writing and states that all matters contained in the application are true to the person's knowledge and belief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485.2(6) the person may make a statement in writing instead of swearing an oath` MEANS
    IF `the person uses a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (5)` AND `the statement is in writing and states that all matters contained in the application are true to the person's knowledge and belief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person who uses a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (5) may, instead of swearing an oath, make a statement in writing"

-- src:8755 | Alternative to oath
-- src:8756 | (6) A person who uses a means of telecommunication referred to in subsection (5) may, instead of swearing an oath, make a statement in writing stating that all matters contained in the application are true to their knowledge and belief, and that statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath.
@ref s 485.2(6) (the deeming) (src:8755-8756)
GIVEN `the statement is a statement in writing made under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
