-- 485.2(7) The summons must (a) be directed to the accused or offender; (b) set out briefly the offence ...; and (c) set out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2).
-- src:8757 | Contents of summons
-- src:8758 | (7) The summons must
-- src:8759 | (a) be directed to the accused or offender;
-- src:8760 | (b) set out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged or the offender has been determined to be guilty; and
-- src:8761 | (c) set out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2).
@ref s 485.2(7) (a), (b), (c) (src:8757-8761)
GIVEN `the summons is directed to the accused or offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons sets out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged or the offender has been determined to be guilty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the summons sets out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485.2(7) the summons has the contents required` MEANS
    IF    `the summons is directed to the accused or offender`
      AND `the summons sets out briefly the offence in respect of which the accused is charged or the offender has been determined to be guilty`
      AND `the summons sets out a summary of subsection 145(3), section 512.1 and subsections 524(4) and (6.2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The summons must"

-- 485.2(8) The summons must be served by a peace officer who shall either deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or, if that person cannot conveniently be found,
-- leave it for the person at their latest or usual place of residence with any person found there who appears to be at least 16 years of age.
DECLARE `s 485.2(8) how the summons was served` IS ONE OF
    `s 485.2(8) delivered personally to the person to whom it is directed`
    `s 485.2(8) left at the person's latest or usual place of residence with a person found there`
    `s 485.2(8) served in another way`

-- src:8762 | Service of summons
-- src:8763 | (8) The summons must be served by a peace officer who shall either deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or, if that person cannot conveniently be found, leave it for the person at their latest or usual place of residence with any person found there who appears to be at least 16 years of age.
@ref s 485.2(8) (src:8762-8763)
GIVEN `the summons was served by a peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      how IS A `s 485.2(8) how the summons was served`
      `the person to whom it is directed cannot conveniently be found` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age, in years, the person found at the residence appears to be` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 485.2(8) the summons was served as required` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the summons was served by a peace officer`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The summons must be served by a peace officer"
    ELSE CONSIDER how
         WHEN `s 485.2(8) delivered personally to the person to whom it is directed` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 485.2(8) left at the person's latest or usual place of residence with a person found there` THEN
             IF `the person to whom it is directed cannot conveniently be found` AND `the age, in years, the person found at the residence appears to be` AT LEAST 16
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that person cannot conveniently be found, leave it for the person at their latest or usual place of residence with any person found there who appears to be at least 16 years of age"
         WHEN `s 485.2(8) served in another way` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who shall either deliver it personally to the person to whom it is directed or"
